     Fenton, 14-Jun-2011.)  (Proof modification is discouraged.)
     (New usage is discouraged.) $)
  bdaydmOLD $p |- dom bday = No $=
    ( csur con0 cbday wfo wf bdayfo fof ax-mp fdmi ) ABCABCDABCEFABCGHI $.

  $( The birthday function's range is ` On ` .  (Contributed by Scott Fenton,
     14-Jun-2011.) $)
  bdayrn $p |- ran bday = On $=
    ( csur con0 cbday wfo crn wceq bdayfo forn ax-mp ) ABCDCEBFGABCHI $.

  $( The value of the birthday function is always an ordinal.  (Contributed by
     Scott Fenton, 14-Jun-2011.)  (Proof shortened by Scott Fenton,
     8-Dec-2021.) $)
  bdayon $p |- ( bday ` A ) e. On $=
    ( csur con0 cbday wfo wf bdayfo fof ax-mp 0elon f0cli ) BCADBCDEBCDFGBCDHIJ
    K $.

